```java
@Service
public class OrderService {
    private static final Logger log = LoggerFactory.getLogger(OrderService.class);

    public Order process(Long orderId) {
        try {
            var order = orderRepo.findById(orderId)
                .orElseThrow(() -> new OrderNotFoundException(orderId)); // specific type
            var payment = paymentClient.charge(order.getAmount());
            order.setPaymentId(payment.getId());
            return orderRepo.save(order);
        } catch (PaymentException e) {
            log.error("Payment failed for order {}", orderId, e);                 // log with the exception
            throw new OrderProcessingException("order " + orderId + " failed", e); // wrap with cause
        }
        // Unexpected failures propagate — we don't catch Exception here.
    }
}
```
*Specific `catch`, logged with the exception object, rethrown with the original `PaymentException` as the cause.*

