// Fail-fast validation at the entry point
public Order createOrder(Customer customer, List<Item> items) {
    Objects.requireNonNull(customer, "customer cannot be null");
    Objects.requireNonNull(items, "items cannot be null");
    return new Order(customer, items);
}
```
*`Optional` makes "might be absent" explicit; `requireNonNull` rejects null at the door with a clear message.*

